	(text "LINEAR CURRENT SINK (simulated in sim/laser_sink.py)\nI_laser = V_set / R_sense, with V_set = PWM duty x 3.3 V x R5 / (R4 + R5) (0.206 V at 100%).\nJP1 open (default): R_sense = R1 = 7.5 ohm, config A (Sony SLD3134VL), 27.5 mA full scale.\nJP1 bridged: R_sense = R1 || R6 = 0.68 ohm, config B (Osram PLPT5 447KA), 302 mA full scale.\nBridge JP1 only with an Osram laser fitted: a Sony diode would see 11x its current.\nR4/R5/C2 filter the PWM (tau ~9.4 ms): soft start and brightness control.\nR2 = 470 ohm isolates the LM321 from Q1's gate capacitance (needed for stability).\nNever connect a laser to a powered driver, and keep PWM at 0 while LASER_RAIL changes state.\nJ1 (4-pin from controller): 1 LASER_RAIL, 2 GND, 3 PWM, 4 +5V (atomizer supply)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "07c51c4c-5293-464e-b38c-96221c409545")
	)
